  "id": "facial-electromyography",
  "term": "facial electromyography",
  "definition": "Facial electromyography is a psychophysiological method that measures facial muscle activity to examine how emotions appear in the body. Its very fine time resolution can capture brief facial micro-expressions and track moment-to-moment changes during emotion regulation.",
